          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>The \"Lady with the Lamp\"</strong><br>\nNightingale was known as the \"Lady with the Lamp\" for her nightly rounds to care for wounded soldiers. Her compassion became a symbol of hope and care for those suffering.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Reforms in Nursing</strong><br>\nAfter the war, Nightingale established a nursing school, which transformed nursing into a respectable profession. Her emphasis on sanitation and training inspired worldwide healthcare reforms.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Statistical Advocacy</strong><br>\nNightingale was also an early and influential advocate of medical statistics. She used data to demonstrate the impact of proper nursing care on reducing mortality rates.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
