            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Legacy and Honors</strong><br>\nHer legacy includes the Nightingale Pledge taken by new nurses and the Florence Nightingale Medal, the highest international distinction a nurse can achieve.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Later Life and Death</strong><br>\nIn her later years, Nightingale suffered from ill health but continued to work on public health issues. She died on August 13, 1910, revered as the pioneer of modern nursing.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Posthumous Recognition</strong><br>\nNightingale's contributions to health care have had lasting influence. She is remembered and celebrated for her role in changing the nature of nursing and hospital care.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
